rate videos now with Sora 2 that look like reality or almost like reality, and not everybody out there will see or understand that a certain video is AI. There are people that think that everything they see on TikTok or Instagram is real, and it''s not. And to be very honest, uh, even you and me who got some understanding of what''s going on in the AI space, even we will definitely often be tricked into thinking that something''s real if it''s not, and that can''t be good for humanity. And, uh, I mean, our brains are rotting since, uh, years already with all the short form content, and yeah, now I''m just an old guy. Not that old, I guess, but I grew up without TikTok and Instagram, and I know, I''m just that guy that complains about the- the future and how everything was better in the past, but I''m really worried about where this will all take us, uh, for, yeah, humanity as a whole, as I said. Because our attention spans get shorter and shorter and shorter, there are more fakes out there, there will be lots of people that use those capabilities for bad things, for scams, for fraud of all kinds, so that''s something we have to be worried and yeah, I''m just not sure if that''s all shiny and great. And don''t get me wrong. As I said, there are great use cases, um, being able to produce stock footage, uh, if you''re a video creator with help of great, though, to be fair, there is the entire copyright thing going on. That stock footage or that B-roll, I mean, not stock footage, the B-roll you''re producing, um, is of course, in the end, based on a model that was trained on likely copyrighted material, so that is a whole different thing, but the use case you unlock, being able to generate B-roll that fits your video perfectly, uh, without you searching through stock libraries for hours, that''s great. I won''t lie about that. I see other val- valuable use cases too, though again, you can always also argue if it''s really that valuable that some things get easier when t